Location & Maps Info
Interpreting API Location Data
When using our /v2/server endpoint, with the Players parameter set to true, you’ll receive location data:
{
  "Player": "PlayerName:123456789",
  "Location": {
    "LocationX": -420,
    "LocationZ": 275,
    "PostalCode": "403",
    "StreetName": "Independence Parkway",
    "BuildingNumber": ""
  }
}
These values use the centre of the ER:LC map as their origin:
- 0, 0 is the centre of the map.
- LocationX is the horizontal position. Positive values move right and negative values move left.
- LocationZ is the vertical position. Positive values move down and negative values move up.
Our official map images are 3121 by 3121 pixels.
